> (without the quotes of course)...
> 
>> (WW) Warning, couldn't open module pex5
>> (EE) Failed to load module "pex5" (module does not exist, 0)
> 
> During dpkg-reconfigure, debconf will ask you for the modules to load.
> It appears that pex5 is no longer bundled with X, since it is now
> "superseded by Mesa/OpenGL", so deselect it.
> 
>> (II) Loading /usr/X11R6/lib/modules/fonts/libxtt.a
>> Duplicate symbol TT_FreeType_Version in 
>> /usr/X11R6/lib/modules/fonts/libxtt.a:xttmodule.o
>> Also defined in /usr/X11R6/lib/modules/fonts/libfreetype.a
> 
> Both "xtt" and "freetype" are modules that handle the rendering of
> TrueType fonts and may thus conflict with each other. Depending on
> various factors (e.g. the font server in use, existence or not of
> truetype fonts in your system, etc.) you may or may not need any of
> them. In any case, don't select them both.
